  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nA weak cold front continues to approach from western and\nnorthern NY with some clouds over the North Country and\nAdirondacks this afternoon. A sfc pressure gradient between the\ncold front and the mid-level short-wave to the west/northwest \nand Subtropical Storm Josephine moving northeast into the \nAtlantic has allowed for north/northwest winds 5-15 mph with \nsome gusts 20-25 mph especially south and east of the Capital \nRegion. The winds will gradually diminish tonight, as the sfc \ncold front washes out. Light north/northwest winds may persist \nafter midnight from the Capital Region south and east, as the \nsfc high builds in from southeast Ontario and southern Quebec. \nWith the weak low-level cold advection lows fall back into the \n30s with some upper 20s over the higher terrain. \n\nA strong sfc anticyclone builds in over eastern NY and western\nNew England tomorrow, and lasts through the weekend. The strong\nsubsidence from the ridge will yield mostly sunny conditions.\nPWATs will run 1-2 STDEVs below normal in the dry air mass.\nShallow mixing heights and weak cold advection will yield \nslightly below normal temps with highs in the upper 40s to mid \nand spotty upper 50s for Fri. The sfc high over southern \nQuebec, NY and New England will yield ideal radiational cooling \nconditions with mostly clear skies, light to calm winds with \nlows in the 20s with a few upper teens over the southern Dacks\nFri night. We went below the NBM guidance for lows going closer\nto the MAV/MET guidance. High pressure remains dominate for the\nweekend with temps modifying to seasonal to slightly above \nnormal temps with light winds. Ideal radiational cooling is \nexpected again Sat night with chilly temps. The mid and upper \nlevel heights begin to fall Sun night into Mon as the the flow \naloft becomes more zonal which will allow temps to run near to \nslight above normal. The next chance of rainfall looks like \npotentially Wed into Thu with a short-wave and a warm front, but\nprecipitation looks light in the medium range/ensemble/NBM \nguidance.",
